\par\par \b \uc2 POLL -Bearishness towards yuan, rupee ebbs; rises for other Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 753 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2015\par 09:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Short positions in most Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit 1-month highs\par     * Singapore dollar bearish bets nearly double\par     * Yuan and rupee short positions cut to 2-month low\par \par     By Masayuki Kitano\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Investors increased bearish\par bets on most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the last two weeks\par after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials kept open the possibility of an\par interest rate hike in 2015 and as worries of a global economic\par slowdown lingered.\par     Short positions in the South Korean won,\par Singapore dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan\par dollar, Malaysian ringgit, Philippine peso\par  and the Thai baht all rose to the largest\par levels since early September.    \par     Persistent worries of a slowdown in Chinese and global\par growth have weighed on share markets round the world and\par dampened risk sentiment in the past couple of weeks.\par     The lingering possibility of a Fed rate hike later this year\par has also weighed on Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  had said last week that\par she expects the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to begin raising interest\par rates later this year as long as inflation remains stable and\par the U.S. economy is strong enough to boost employment.\par  \par     The ringgit and the rupiah both plumbed 17-year lows earlier\par this week, while the Singapore dollar set a six-year low and the\par Thai baht hit its lowest level in more than eight years.\par     Bearish bets on the Singapore dollar nearly doubled, as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faces headwinds from  expectations that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  will ease monetary policy in mid-October.\par  \par     There were also relatively large increases in short\par positions in the South Korean won and the Taiwan dollar.\par     Meantime, investors trimmed bearish bets against the Chinese\par yuan to the lowest level since early August.\par     Investors have turned bearish on the yuan in the wake of\par China's surprise \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation in August, having been\par bullish previously.\par     The yuan, however, has stabilised over the past few weeks,\par buoyed by suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     Besides the yuan, investors also pared bearish bets on the \par Indian rupee to the smallest level in two months. \par     Indian share markets rose after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par cut its policy interest rate to a 4-1/2 year low of 6.75 percent\par on Tuesday, in a bigger-than-expected move that could help turn\par around an economy that has been slowing down. \par     The poll is focused on what analysts and fund managers\par believe are the current market positions in nine Asian emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese yuan, South Korean won, Singapore\par dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan dollar, Indian rupee,\par Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit and the Thai baht.\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3. A score of plus 3 indicates the\par market is significantly long U.S. dollars.\par     The figures include positions held through non-deliverable\par forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):                           \par              \par  DATE     CNY   KRW   SGD   IDR   TWD   INR   MYR   PHP   THB\par  1-Oct    0.13  1.01  1.20  1.35  1.04  0.11  1.71  0.68  1.20\par  17-Sept  0.26  0.60  0.62  1.27  0.73  0.27  1.48  0.54  1.00\par  3-Sept   0.62  1.09  1.31  1.45  1.15  0.66  1.96  0.86  1.51\par  20-Aug   0.91  1.56  1.50  1.55  1.58  0.75  2.21  1.04  1.86\par  6-Aug   -0.15  1.27  1.19  1.16  0.91  0.11  1.82  0.84  1.40\par  23-July -0.50  1.32  0.97  0.69  0.70  0.09  1.24  0.52  1.18\par  9-July  -0.13  1.09  0.38  0.78  0.56 -0.06  1.33  0.37  0.80\par  25-June -0.70  0.29  0.22  0.80  0.11 -0.26  1.10  0.30  0.57\par  11-June -0.47  0.77  0.61  1.12  0.48  0.05  1.39  0.43  0.69\par  28-May  -0.62  0.67  0.53  1.05  0.02  0.29  0.86  0.03  0.89\par  14-May  -0.45  0.11 -0.05  0.95 -0.30  0.22  0.41 -0.06  0.78\par  \par  (Additional reporting by Shaloo Shrivastava in BENGALURU;\par Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-10-1T08:06:16.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020151001eba1007sl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
