\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2015\par 14:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. Warplanes Carry Out Airstrike in Northern Afghanistan \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Airstrike came in support of Afghan government forces attempting to retake control of the city of Kunduz from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taliban\f28 \uc2 \f2  fighters. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Eurozone Confidence Firms, Inflation Worries Revive \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Businesses and households across the eurozone were mostly untroubled in September by the prospect of slower growth in China, and warnings from central bankers that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area's modest recovery could weaken as a consequence. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU to Rule Quickly on European, U.S. Data Pact \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 's highest court confirmed it would decide early next week on a highly publicized case that could invalidate a data pact between the EU and the U.S. that is critical to thousands of businesses. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Yuan's Short-Term Rates Spike in Hong Kong \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sees highest borrowing costs in a month as banks hold onto cash ahead of Chinese holiday and after \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Caps Overseas Cash Withdrawals \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has capped the amount of money Chinese holders of bank and credit cards can withdraw outside the country, in its latest effort to discourage people from moving badly needed capital offshore. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par India's RBI Cuts Key Interest Rate More Than Expected \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its key interest rate more than markets expected and for the fourth time this year amid optimism Indian inflation rates will remain low. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Catalonia's President to Face Court Questioning Over Independence Vote \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A court in Catalonia summoned regional leader Artur Mas for questioning next month for allegedly defying a constitutional court order and organizing a vote on Catalan independence. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Parties in Iran Nuclear Deal Aim for Implementation in Early 2016 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign ministers from Iran and the six powers that negotiated July's nuclear agreement met to discuss the implementation of the deal, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  foreign policy chief Federica Mogherini saying they hope to complete that work in early 2016. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Cameron Says Migrant Crisis Complicates U.K. Debate on EU \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 David Cameron\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Europe's migrant crisis is complicating his efforts to change Britain's relationship with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , something he has promised the British public he would do. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Australia's Turnbull Calls Reform Summit \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New leader seeks input from businesses, unions and the community on controversial tax changes in hope of avoiding recession.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 29, 2015 08:02 ET (12:02 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150929eb9t001es\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
