\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan inches up on firmer midpoint fix, suspected c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2015\par 06:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 29 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan inched up against\par the dollar on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a firmer\par midpoint and was also suspected of selling dollars via state\par banks to support the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.366 per dollar prior to market open, 0.11 percent firmer\par than the previous fix at 6.3729. \par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to be persistently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par this morning by selling dollars," said a trader at a Chinese\par commercial bank in Shanghai.\par     The strong fix and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  supported the yuan in spot\par market trade. It opened at 6.3657 per dollar and was\par changing hands at 6.3641 at midday, 0.08 percent firmer than the\par previous close. \par     The onshore yuan was also buoyed by the overnight strength\par of the offshore yuan on broad dollar weakness, traders said.\par     The offshore yuan, trading at 6.3695 per dollar by\par midday, slipped 0.2 percent on Tuesday after gaining 0.6 percent\par overnight.\par     That pushed the discount of the offshore yuan against the\par onshore yuan to only 0.08 percent, the least since the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chinese\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  abruptly devaluated the yuan in mid-August.\par     The discount had widened to nearly 2 percent in the days\par following the devaluation because of widespread expectations of\par more downside for the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the long run.\par     \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.366    6.3729    0.11%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3641   6.369     0.08%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    -0.03%             \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.52%\par  Spot change since 2005                30.05%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.3695    -0.08%\par           *                      \par  Offshore              6.579     -3.24%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     GRAPHICS:\par     The yuan in trade-weighted terms \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     The spot market versus the trading band \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Shri\par Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-29T05:59:48.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150929eb9t005sw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
