\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan firms on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  as c.bank keeps yuan stable\b0\par\par\uc2 540 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2015\par 06:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 24 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed on\par Thursday as state-owned banks sold dollars on behalf of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , offsetting a slightly weaker official guidance\par rate.\par     Traders said that they saw a relatively large amount of\par dollar sales by the state-owned banks. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par typically uses these banks to trade on behalf of itself to\par influence the yuan's value.\par     "The midpoint is only set slightly weaker today," said a\par trader at a Chinese commercial bank in Shanghai.\par     "Plus signs of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trading, the\par market believes the authorities may want to keep the yuan stable\par in the near term."\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint rate\par  at 6.3791 per dollar prior to market open, 0.03\par percent weaker than the previous fix of 6.3773. \par     In the spot market, the yuan opened at 6.3829 per\par dollar and was changing hands at 6.3793 at midday, 0.07 percent\par firmer than the previous close.\par     Trader said that they believed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would hold\par the yuan around 6.38.\par     Despite Thursday's activity, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has generally scaled\par back onshore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent weeks, following a\par rapid-fire series of support moves after its surprise\par devaluation of the yuan in mid-August.\par     The devaluation triggered intense speculation that the\par government would allow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken further to help\par struggling exporters, though top officials have repeatedly said\par they see no basis for more depreciation.\par     In a related development, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  raised the ceiling on\par cross-border fund flows for multinationals via two-way\par cross-border yuan cash pooling and lowered the threshold for\par participation in the business. \par     The cash pooling allows multinationals to more conveniently\par allocate capital between group companies, enhancing cash\par management efficiency and cuts financing costs.\par     The offshore yuan was trading 0.84 percent weaker than the\par onshore spot at 6.4332 per dollar. \par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts\par , considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 6.6105, or 3.50 percent weaker than Thursday's the midpoint.\par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.3791   6.3773    -0.03%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3793   6.3839    0.07%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.00%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.75%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.74%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.4332    -0.84%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.6105    -3.50%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     GRAPHICS:\par     The yuan in trade-weighted terms \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     The spot market versus the trading band \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-24T05:26:52.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150924eb9o004v8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
