\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan softens on firmer dollar, reduced  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 ; offshore volatile\b0\par\par\uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2015\par 06:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 23 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan weakened on\par Wednesday as the dollar strengthened in global markets while\par scaled-back \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par onshore market has permitted the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to soften of\par late, traders said.\par     Offshore yuan was volatile after a run of data showed that\par Chinese economic growth continued slowing in September.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.3773\par per dollar prior to market open, 0.08 percent weaker than the\par previous fix 6.3721. \par     The spot market opened at 6.3799 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.3833 at midday, 0.11 percent weaker than\par the previous close.\par     "The authorities seemed to accept a moderate depreciation of\par yuan more recently," said a trader at a Chinese commercial bank\par in Shanghai.\par     That lenience has allowed the yuan to move more in line with\par market supply and demand this week, the trader and others said.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  scaled back \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid comments on Tuesday\par by Chinese President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xi Jinping\f28 \uc2 \f2  that China would push forward\par market-based reform of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime and make the yuan\par convertible on the capital account over time. \par     Later that day, banking industry sources told Reuters that\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had completed drafting regulations for an\par international payment system that would facilitate greater usage\par of the yuan globally. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped up its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in yuan trading\par for a few weeks to cushion the economy against the unexpected\par aftermath of its abrupt devaluation of the yuan in mid-August.\par     The offshore yuan was nearly flat at midday at\par 6.421, but still trading 0.59 percent weaker than onshore spot.\par     The offshore yuan initially weakened by 0.24 percent around\par the mid-morning trade after the release of the preliminary\par Caixin/Markit China Manufacturing Purchasing Managers' Index in\par September, which fell to 47 - the worst since March 2009.\par  \par     Traders, however, said that the survey's findings had little\par impact on the onshore market as the outcome was widely expected.\par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts\par , considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 6.5985, or 3.35 percent weaker than Wednesday's the midpoint.\par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.3773   6.3721    -0.08%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3833   6.376     -0.11%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.09%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.81%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.66%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.421     -0.59%\par           *                      \par  Offshore              6.5985    -3.35%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     GRAPHICS:\par     The yuan in trade-weighted terms \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     The spot market versus the trading band \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-23T05:26:03.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150923eb9n005br\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
