\par\par \uc2 Asiastox\par \b \uc2 Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Slide After Fed Officials Signal Rate Increase Possible in 2015\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chao Deng  \par \uc2 935 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2015\par 03:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top Global Market Stories\par \uc2 DJTGMS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened Tuesday after \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  officials suggested interest rates could be raised {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/dollar-advances-as-fed-speakers-signal-interest-rate-increase-still-possible-in-2015-1442854027"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as early as next month  }}}\uc2 , but the region's major stock markets gained modestly ahead of a reading on Chinese manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit fell by 0.5% against the U.S. dollar while the Thai baht and Indonesian rupiah each fell by about 0.3%.\par \par \uc2 The Shanghai Composite Index gained 0.9%, leading most of the region higher. As Chinese President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  makes his first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/china-leaders-u-s-trip-includes-stop-on-memory-lane-1442509680"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state visit to the U.S.  }}}\uc2 , the benchmark is down 38% from its June peak, after a selloff that rattled global markets in August. In his first interview with foreign media since the skid began, Mr. Xi said that the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its stock market was necessary to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/despite-slump-chinas-xi-pledges-economic-reforms-1442894460"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "defuse systemic risks."  }}}\uc2 , the benchmark is down 38% from its June peak, after a selloff that rattled global markets in August. In his first interview with foreign media since the skid began, Mr. Xi said that the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its stock market was necessary to\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nearly 2% devaluation of the yuan, which had investors questioning whether the slowdown in China's domestic economy was worse than previously thought, Mr. Xi said that said the reduction in foreign reserves that followed is normal "and there's no need to overreact to it."\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  closed up 0.2%. Shares in Southeast Asia, though, were down, as their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell. Indonesia's JSX was off 0.6%.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose overnight to levels reached before last week's Fed decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/fed-leaves-interest-rates-unchanged-1442512974"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leave interest rates unchanged  }}}\uc2 . Regional Fed presidents \uc2 Jeffrey Lacker\uc2  of Richmond, Va., \uc2 James Bullard\uc2  of St. Louis and \uc2 John Williams\uc2  of San Francisco signaled in speeches that many \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  objectives had been met and that Thursday's decision was a close call.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which measures the dollar against a basket of 16 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rose overnight to its highest level since Sept. 10, at 88.49 overnight. It was last at 88.33.\par \par \uc2 "The reinstatement of long positions in the U.S. dollar is helping calm Asian stock markets [and] easing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Evan Lucas, a strategist at brokerage IG.\par \par \uc2 Stock trading in the region has been relatively muted this week, with Japanese markets shut for a national holiday until Thursday. "It makes things more cautious in terms of trading," Mr. Lucas said.\par \par \uc2 Investors are looking to a reading on Chinese manufacturing activity for September, due Wednesday from Caixin Media Co. and research firm \uc2 Markit Ltd\uc2 . The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/china-august-manufacturing-pmi-slips-1441070881"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August reading  }}}\uc2  was the lowest in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/china-august-manufacturing-pmi-slips-1441070881"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than six years  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Worse-than-expected economic growth in the first half for most Asian economies and a delayed global recovery led the \uc2 Asian Development Bank\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/asian-development-banks-regional-gloom-deepens-1442900588"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut its regional forecasts  }}}\uc2  for this year and next. The region's GDP will grow 5.8% in 2015 and 6.0% in 2016\u8212\'20\'14down in both cases from 6.3% previously forecast\u8212\'20\'14the Manila-based development lender said in a report Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In the latest assessment on China, ADB cut that country's growth forecast to 6.8% from 7.2% and said that developing Asian economies closely linked with China need to explore "new avenues," adjusting to slower Chinese growth driven more by domestic consumption and less by investment.\par \par \uc2 The report followed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/s-p-says-chinas-banks-face-growing-risk-from-bad-debt-1442837903"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downgrade of China's banking industry  }}}\uc2  Monday by U.S. credit-rating firm \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  Ratings Services, which cut the outlook to negative from stable. \uc2 S&P\uc2  said China's banks, one of Beijing's major levers as it tries to lift growth in the world's second-largest economy, face growing risk tied to rising bad loans and problems in its real-estate sector.\par \par \uc2 South Korea's Kospi gained 0.9%. Australia's S&P/ASX 200 was up 0.7%, bouncing from its sharpest loss in more than a week. The benchmark had lost 2% Monday, weighed down by anxiety about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/shares-in-asia-fall-on-worries-about-global-growth-1442798710"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pace of global growth  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Australia's mining and energy shares have been dented by global-growth worries at a time when several of the country's biggest commodity exports have excess supplies. Banking stocks have also sold off amid worries about the local economy, which some analysts say may be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/is-australia-sliding-into-recession-1441091988"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 headed for a recession  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Australian market is trading near its lowest levels since 2013, the victim with other Asia-Pacific markets of that selloff in China last month. The S&P/ASX 200 bottomed out at 5001.28 in late August and is currently off 15% from its April peak.\par \par \uc2 But on Tuesday, shares across the board gained in Australia, with energy stocks standing out after oil prices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/oil-prices-climb-as-production-capacity-falls-1442832460"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bounced back overnight  }}}\uc2 . Light, sweet crude for October delivery settled up $2, or 4.5%, at $46.68 a barrel, on expectations that a drop in U.S. production would help shrink the domestic glut of crude.\par \par \uc2 "Yesterday's move was a big overreaction," said IG's Mr. Lucas, explaining that volume in Australia's stock market was 30% below the 30-day average. "You can't take yesterday at face value," he said, adding, "you're seeing a bit of correction" today.\par \par \uc2 Brent oil was last down 1.4% at $48.23 a barrel from its level late Monday in Asia.\par \par \uc2 Gold was up 0.2% at $1134.90 a troy ounce.\par \par \uc2 Charles Hutzler, Anjani Trivedi and James Ramage contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Chao Deng at \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTGMS1120150922eb9m00011\par }\page {\par\