\par\par \b \uc2 CNH TRACKER-Dim sum bond market seen to get a boost from stable  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michelle Chen   \par \uc2 798 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2015\par 09:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Sept 17 (Reuters) - Beijing's attempts to stabilise the yuan should boost the sluggish offshore yuan bond market, after the damage inflicted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness in the wake of last month's devaluation.\par \par \uc2 The offshore yuan shot higher suddenly last Thursday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by state banks and it has been hovering around 6.4 per dollar. The spread between onshore and offshore spots has narrowed to around 300 pips from more than 1,000 pips.\par \par \uc2 "Our yuan bond funds will benefit from the appreciation in the short term and investors' appetite for yuan assets is likely to come back if CNH \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate stays close to CNY," said a fund manager in Hong Kong who invests in dim sum bonds.\par \par \uc2 Investors would prefer to buy yuan bonds issued in the mainland instead of those in Hong Kong as the onshore yuan is stronger than the offshore yuan, but the good thing is that the gap between the two rates has narrowed, the fund manager said.\par \par \uc2 The primary offshore yuan bond market has lost growth momentum this year since Chinese financial institutions and companies that used to be dominant issuers switched to the onshore market to raise cheaper funds.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2 's (\uc2 PBOC\uc2 ) devaluation of the yuan on Aug. 11 has added to the pressure on dim sum bonds as investors sold yuan assets to avoid further \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses.\par \par \uc2 Dim sum bond issuance in August fell to 7.5 billion yuan($1.18 billion), the lowest monthly volume in two years, according to Thomson Reuters statistics. Issuance in the first eight months declined by 45 percent from a year ago.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 HSBC\uc2  offshore yuan bond index showed that these bonds' performance in August fell by 2.6 percent from a month earlier, the biggest monthly drop since June 2013 when index declined by 2.8 percent.\par \par \uc2 But thanks to the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the secondary dim sum market became more active as new funds were gradually coming in to seek opportunities, said Penny Chen, a fixed-income fund manager at Manulife Asset Management in Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 "There is a bigger than needed risk premium on offshore yuan bonds that is being attached now in light of the recent market turmoil which offers us opportunities," said Bryan Collins, who manages $5 billion in assets at Fidelity Worldwide Investment.\par \par \uc2 Bets on further weakness in China's yuan fell by more than half in the last two weeks as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after its surprise devaluation last month, a Reuters poll showed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts, however, remain cautious about the yuan's prospect in the coming year, with some of the most bearish ones, such as Kevin Lai, Daiwa's Asia ex-Japan chief economist, expecting it to fall to 7.5 per dollar by the end of next year.\par \par \uc2 WEEK IN REVIEW:\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong's yuan deposits and certificates of deposits (CDs) is expected to fall in the short term as some investors have converted the yuan to Hong Kong dollar or U.S. dollar, Norman Chan, the chief executive of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 * China's top economic planner on Wednesday told Chinese firms with good credit to issue bonds in cheaper offshore markets to support domestic investment and major national projects.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commercial banks sold a net 723.8 billion yuan ($113.69 billion) of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August, by far the largest on record, highlighting how capital outflows intensified in the wake of the yuan's devaluation last month.\par \par \uc2 * China will allow foreign central banks to trade in its spot interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and trade \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives such as swaps and forwards, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 has increased the quota for net yuan inflows under a cross-border pooling scheme that enables companies to transfer the yuan between their onshore and offshore entities freely, two sources told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 CHART OF THE WEEK:\par \par \uc2 Performance of offshore yuan bonds lags peers in the region: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zaw35t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zaw35t}}}\par \par \uc2 RECENT STORIES: Hong Kong yuan deposits seen falling despite \b \highlight22\uc2 China FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilisation efforts \b \highlight22\uc2 China central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if offshore pushes yuan too far \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's clamp down on speculators in yuan forwards set to hit importers too\par \par \uc2 \f2 More stories about the CNH market                 \par Daily onshore yuan reports                        \par Daily China money market reports                  \par   \par Offshore yuan rate    Onshore yuan rate  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Offshore yuan dealt Onshore yuan on CFETS THOMSON REUTERS SPEED GUIDES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Saikat Chatterjee; Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore) \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-17T08:38:54.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150917eb9h008kh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
