\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan flat on c.bank's  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  after early weakening\b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2015\par 05:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 16 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan weakened\par Wednesday morning but was almost unchanged against the dollar at\par midday after state-owned banks bought the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on behalf of\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stabilise its rate, traders said.\par     "There are persistent small amounts of yuan purchases from\par state-owned banks on Wednesday," said a trader at a Chinese\par commercial bank.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.3712 per dollar prior to market open, 0.07 percent weaker\par than the previous fix 6.3665. \par     The yuan hit an intraday low of 6.3744 in early\par trade in line with the slightly weakened midpoint, but it\par rebounded after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Its intraday high of 6.3692\par was not far away from the midday level.\par     "I think the yuan will sustain at around 6.37 due to the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , moving within 100 points in either\par side," the trader said.\par     The offshore yuan was trading 0.57 percent weaker\par than the onshore spot at 6.406 per dollar. \par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts \par , considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 6.5935, or 3.37 percent weaker than Wednesday's midpoint.\par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.3712   6.3665    -0.07%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3696   6.37      0.01%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    -0.03%             \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.60%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.94%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.406     -0.57%\par           *                      \par  Offshore              6.5935    -3.37%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     GRAPHICS:\par     The yuan in trade-weighted terms \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     The spot market versus the trading band \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Richard Borsuk)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-16T04:35:22.000Z   \