\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan firms as suspected c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  offsets outflow pressure\b0\par\par\uc2 496 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2015\par 06:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 14 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan erased early\par losses and firmed on Monday afternoon, supported by suspected\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  via yuan-purchases by\par state-owned banks, traders said.\par     The suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  offset the early losses on the\par yuan, which were possibly triggered by a Sunday report from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par for International Settlements\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BIS) that capital outflows in\par Chinese banks in the first quarter of 2015 and weak incentives\par to hold yuan positions indicated capital may keep trickling out.\par  \par     Pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from fund outflows has increased \par since the surprise devaluation of the yuan on Aug. 11.   \par     "There is a relatively large amount of yuan purchases this\par morning," said a trader at a foreign bank in Shanghai. "There\par are signs that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  maybe hoping to guide the yuan\par to around 6.36."\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint rate\par  at 6.3709 per dollar prior to market open, 0.02\par percent firmer than the previous fix at 6.3719. \par     The spot market opened at 6.3760 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.3699 at midday, 0.08 percent higher than\par the previous close.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has ordered Chinese commercial banks to require\par their clients to provide justification for purchases of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  using yuan, and ensure the foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par deposited in offshore accounts or special designated accounts\par onshore, sources told Reuters on Friday. \par     Traders said they believed that the new instructions on NRA\par would reduce onshore and offshore arbitrage opportunities and\par help keep the yuan stable.\par     The offshore yuan was trading 0.5 percent weaker\par than the onshore spot at 6.4022 per dollar. \par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts\par , considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 6.58, or 3.18 percent weaker than Monday's midpoint.\par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.3709   6.3719    0.02%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3699   6.375     0.08%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    -0.02%             \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.60%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.93%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.4022    -0.50%\par           *                      \par  Offshore              6.58      -3.18%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     GRAPHICS:\par     The yuan in trade-weighted terms \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     The spot market versus the trading band \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Shri\par Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-14T05:35:10.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150914eb9e003sf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
