\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yuan rebound supports Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , weekly regional losses seen\b0\par\par\uc2 862 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2015\par 08:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan up on firmer midpoint, offshore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * Won rises; \f28 \uc2 \f2 S.Korea c.bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  holds rates\par     * Ringgit, rupiah lead weekly Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  losses\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 11 - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on\par Friday, tracking the Chinese yuan's rebound, though most of\par regional units were set to post weekly losses on worries about a\par worsening slowdown in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The yuan advanced after suspected rare\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in offshore market by Chinese state banks to\par support the renminbi on Thursday lifted it more than 1 percent,\par the offshore rate's largest daily gain on record.\par  The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday also fixed its daily\par guidance rate firmer. \par     South Korea's won strengthened on demand from\par offshore funds. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  noted that another rate cut\par soon was unlikely due to an economic recovery, although some\par economists expected a reduction later this year. \par     The ringgit gained in thin trading as overnight\par rebounds in oil prices eased concerns over Malaysian exports of\par liquefied natural gas and palm oil.\par     Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lost some of their gains as caution set\par in ahead of the release of Chinese economic data on Sunday\par including output.\par     Uncertainty over whether the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would raise\par interest rates at its Sept. 16-17 Federal Open Market Committee\par (FOMC) meeting also encouraged caution. \par     "\f28 \uc2 \f2 The Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  may hike... or not. Neither scenario is likely to\par be supportive of a more constructive view on EM assets,"\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a research note, referring to emerging markets.\par     "Regardless of the outcome of the FOMC meeting, EM\par performance should be weighed down by China uncertainty, slowing\par growth, capital outflows and - as evidenced by this week's\par Brazil downgrade - rating risks."\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday downgraded Brazil to a "junk"\par credit rating, with the economy and public finances\par deteriorating amid falling commodity prices and China's\par slowdown. \par     \par     RUPIAH, RINGGIT HIT\par     In emerging Asia, commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  led weekly regional\par losses with the ringgit and the Indonesian rupiah \par falling to their weakest levels since the Asian financial crisis\par 17 years ago.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost 1.3 percent against the\par dollar so far this week although the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves unexpectedly rose slightly in the last two weeks of\par August. \par     The increase in came as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not seen\par defending specific levels of the ringgit, traders and analysts\par said. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  may have spent less supporting the\par ringgit than it had done earlier as the market was thin, traders\par added.\par     The rupiah has slid 1.1 percent throughout this week,\par ignoring fresh economic stimulus to lure more investment, boost\par consumer spending and support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The yuan has slumped 0.3 percent so far this week despite\par Beijing's efforts to quell speculators betting against the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . That would be the first weekly loss since the week of\par the surprising devaluation on Aug. 11, according to Thomson\par Reuters data.\par     The suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the yuan in the\par offshore market showed Beijing's desire to stabilise the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said.\par     "The move on Thursday is a move to stabilise the yuan and\par ease capital outflows," said Yuna Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond\par analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul, referring to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the offshore market.\par     "It does not mean that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is driving the yuan stronger."\par     Thailand's baht has weakened 0.6 percent so far\par this week, while the Philippine peso has eased 0.2\par percent.\par     By contrast, the won has risen 0.8 percent throughout this\par week as dollar demand stemming from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tesco\f28 \uc2 \f2 's $6/1\par billion sale of its South Korean arm to a group led by a\par Seoul-based private equity firm appeared to be over.\par  \par     Expectations of rising dollar demand resulting from the deal\par had pushed the won to a five-year low earlier this week.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0540 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       120.72         120.61       -0.09\par  *Sing dlr        1.4132         1.4135       +0.02\par   Taiwan dlr      32.515         32.856       +1.05\par   Korean won     1184.29        1194.40       +0.85\par   Baht             36.07          36.13       +0.16\par   Peso             46.84          46.85       +0.03\par   Rupiah        14313.00       14330.00       +0.12\par   Rupee            66.37          66.43       +0.09\par   Ringgit         4.3100         4.3370       +0.63\par   Yuan            6.3732         6.3772       +0.06\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       120.72         119.66       -0.88\par   Sing dlr        1.4132         1.3260       -6.17\par   Taiwan dlr      32.515         31.718       -2.45\par   Korean won     1184.29        1099.30       -7.18\par   Baht             36.07          32.90       -8.80\par   Peso             46.84          44.72       -4.52\par   Rupiah        14313.00       12380.00      -13.51\par   Rupee            66.37          63.03       -5.03\par   Ringgit         4.3100         3.4965      -18.87\par   Yuan            6.3732         6.2040       -2.65\par   * Financial markets in Singapore are closed for a general\par election.\par \par  (Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-11T07:14:13.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150911eb9b006q2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
