\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan eases on weaker midpoint, less c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2015\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 10 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan weakened against\par the dollar on Thursday in line with a weaker midpoint, while the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less heavily in the\par market via state-owned banks.\par     "State banks sold a small quantity of dollars sporadically\par on Thursday, changing into mild support compared with aggressive\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the previous few weeks," said a\par trader at a commercial bank in Shanghai.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.3772 per dollar prior to market open, 0.22 percent weaker\par than the previous fix of 6.3632. \par     The spot market opened at 6.3825 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.3846 at midday, 0.11 percent weaker than\par the previous close.\par     Traders said the yuan was likely to fluctuate between 50 and\par 100 points in a day in the near term. \par     The 6.4 level is where the market believes the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par may resume intensified \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \par     As a sign of weak sentiment towards the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par offshore yuan was trading 1.3 percent weaker than the\par onshore spot at 6.4687 per dollar. \par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts\par , considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 6.657, or 4.2 percent weaker than Thursday's midpoint.\par     \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.3772   6.3632    -0.22%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3846   6.3778    -0.11%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.12%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.83%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.63%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.4687    -1.30%\par           *                      \par  Offshore              6.657     -4.20%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     GRAPHICS:\par     The yuan in trade-weighted terms \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     The spot market versus the trading band \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi"}}{\fldrslt{\c