\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 874 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2015\par 16:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. STOCKS RALLY, TAKING \f28 \uc2 \f2 CUES\f28 \uc2 \f2  FROM OVERSEAS MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks rallied after the Labor Day holiday, following gains in Europe and China. Some investors said markets had started to adjust to worries over a slowdown in China. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EU APPROVES \f28 \uc2 \f2 GE\f28 \uc2 \f2 'S ACQUISITION OF \f28 \uc2 \f2 ALSTOM\f28 \uc2 \f2 'S ENERGY BUSINESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Electric\f28 \uc2 \f2  won approval from Europe's top antitrust authority for its acquisition of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alstom\f28 \uc2 \f2 's power business after the U.S. industrial giant agreed to sell assets that regulators hope will create a strong new competitor in Europe. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MYLAN TO TAKE \f28 \uc2 \f2 PERRIGO\f28 \uc2 \f2  BID TO SHAREHOLDERS MONDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mylan plans to bring its takeover bid for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Perrigo\f28 \uc2 \f2  directly to the company's shareholders on Monday, after being publicly rebuffed since April. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROZONE ECONOMIC GROWTH REVISED HIGHER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The eurozone economy grew more rapidly than previously estimated in the three months to June, as a pickup in exports offset a slowdown in household consumption and a decline in investment spending. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MEDIA GENERAL\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO BUY MEREDITH CORP. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Media General\f28 \uc2 \f2  agreed to buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 Meredith Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for about $2.4 billion in cash and stock in a deal that would create the third-largest local television station owner in the country. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BLACKSTONE\f28 \uc2 \f2  AGREES TO BUY STRATEGIC HOTELS FOR ABOUT $4 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Strategic Hotels\f28 \uc2 \f2  & Resorts said Tuesday that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Blackstone Real Estate Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2  VIII has agreed to buy the luxury hotel company for about $4 billion. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  ACCEPTS INDONESIA'S RETURN TO OIL GROUP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has notified Indonesia that the country can rejoin the oil-producing group when it next meets in December \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. SMALL-BUSINESS CONFIDENCE IMPROVES A BIT IN AUGUST, NFIB SAYS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Small-business owners' confidence about their economic situation was little changed in August-rising modestly to 95.9 from 95.4 in July-according to an index released Tuesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA'S CONCORDIA HEALTHCARE TO BUY AMDIPHARM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concordia Healthcare agreed to acquire U.K.-based Amdipharm Mercury Ltd. from European private-equity firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cinven\f28 \uc2 \f2  for about $1.2 billion in cash and around $700 million in stock. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par E-TRADE RESTRUCTURES BALANCE SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 E-Trade said it is eliminating all of its $4.4 billion of wholesale funding obligations by quarter-end in an effort to boost its bank balance sheet by removing high-cost funding. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. FINES CAESARS $8 MILLION OVER MONEY-LAUNDERING CONTROLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bankrupt casino company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Caesars Entertainment\f28 \uc2 \f2  agreed to an $8 million civil penalty, admitting it had allowed wealthy patrons to gamble anonymously in private rooms at its flagship Las Vegas casino. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FRANCE NOMINATES NEW GOVERNOR OF THE \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF FRANCE\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French President Fran\u231\'00\'E7 ois Hollande has nominated an experienced French commercial banker to be the next governor of the Bank of France. PRO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. OIL PRICES FALL; BRENT RISES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 International oil benchmarks diverged as U.S. prices caught up with the previous day's drop in Brent crude when U.S. markets were shut for a holiday, but behind the split the market remained focused on a recurring theme, the Chinese slowdown. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RESERVE DROP PARTLY DUE TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday that the record drop of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves in August was partly due to its own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DURCHSLAG IS ANGIE'S LIST PRES., CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Angie's List on Tuesday named former \f28 \uc2 \f2 Best Buy\f28 \uc2 \f2  global and e-commerce executive Scott Durchslag as its chief executive and president, effective immediately. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OECD\f28 \uc2 \f2  LEADING INDICATORS POINT TO FURTHER SLOWDOWNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth is set to slow across a number of the world's largest economies, including China, the U.S. and the U.K., according to leading indicators released by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOFA PUSHES TO KEEP MOYNIHAN'S DUAL ROLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stung by a wave of investor criticism, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2  is stepping up efforts to convince shareholders that Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brian Moynihan\f28 \uc2 \f2  should remain chairman. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ISIS ADVANCES ON SYRIAN BORDER TOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Islamic State\f28 \uc2 \f2  fighters intensified their advance in recent days on a town in northern Syria close to a vital supply route for Syrian rebels near the border with Turkey. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KEY JAPAN INFLATION MEASURE LIKELY ACCELERATED IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's preferred measure of inflation likely marked the sharpest gain in about a year and a half in July, despite an increasingly listless economy, people familiar with the calculation said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SUNEDISON TO BUY 33% INTEREST IN DOMINION PORTFOLIO OF SOLAR ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SunEdison Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . agreed to acquire a 33% interest in a portfolio of solar assets from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dominion Resources Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for roughly $300 million, the latest in a recent string of deals between the companies. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par  \par Moneybeat Blog \par U.S. STOCKS TRYING TO BUCK SEPTEMBER'S DOUR HISTORY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This is still a market looking over its shoulder at all the damage done in August. Unless and until the market proves that it is past that weakness, all these rallies are suspect. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Wealth Management Journal \par GROUP OF MERRILL ADVISERS LEAVES TO FORM FIRM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A team of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  financial advisers who manage more than $1 billion have resigned to form an advisory firm to offer more specialized services to clients, such as paying bills and providing advice on customized investments. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 08, 2015 10:28 ET (14:28 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150908eb980022o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
