\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserve Drop Partly Due to \uc2 PBOC \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2015\par 16:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BEIJING--\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday that the record drop of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in August was partly due to its own \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as increased demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Chinese companies and individual investors.\par \par \uc2 In its first public statement since reporting Monday that the reserves fell $93.9 billion, to $3.56 trillion, in August, the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  cited "multiple factors," including its own market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , price fluctuations in reserve assets, and movements of other foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For the reserves, the drop was the largest monthly fall on record. It came as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively bought the yuan and sold dollars to prevent the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from slipping further and capital leaving the country following a surprise 2% devaluation.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement, which was posted on its website, said its moves provided more foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity to the market. It also said that increased \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings by domestic enterprises and individual investors also contributed to the plunge of the official reserves.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in a separate statement, the bank said that the reserve requirement it imposed on banks engaged in trading of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards last week doesn't amount to "capital controls," but is a way to reduce speculation on the yuan.\par \par \uc2 Overall, the bank said, the Chinese economy is still growing at a fast pace and the market remains attractive to global investors. As the yuan exchange rate becomes more market-based, the bank said, it will be "normal" to see ups and downs in China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 Grace Zhu\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 08-09-15 1424GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150908eb98000fc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
