\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan weakens despite firmer midpoint, less  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2015\par 06:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 7 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan weakened against\par the dollar on Monday in spite of a firmer midpoint, as investors\par sold the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen to be\par less heavily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market via state-owned banks.\par     "Dollar sales by state-owned banks on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eased today," said a dealer at a European bank in Shanghai.\par     "As the market still lacks confidence in the yuan's value in\par the future, banks and their clients priced the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaker,\par taking advantage of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's eased \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint rate\par  at 6.3584 per dollar prior to market open, slightly\par firmer than the previous fix of 6.3619. \par     The spot market opened at 6.3560 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.3673 at midday, 0.19 percent weaker than\par the previous close last Wednesday. The market was closed on\par Thursday and Friday for a holiday to mark 70 years after the end\par of World War Two.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised markets on Aug. 11 by devaluing\par the yuan by nearly 2 percent, which sparked sharp selling that\par forced it to come back into the market to dump dollars to\par stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Traders said the yuan could easily depreciate to 6.4 versus\par the dollar if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  stayed on the sidelines.\par     As a sign of weak sentiment towards the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par the offshore yuan was trading 1.42 percent weaker than onshore\par spot at 6.4593 per dollar by midday on Monday.\par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts\par , considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 6.6325, or 4.13 percent weaker than Monday's midpoint.\par     \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.3584   6.3619    0.06%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3678   6.3559    -0.19%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.15%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.57%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.97%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.4593    -1.42%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.6325    -4.13%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     GRAPHICS:\par     The yuan in trade-weighted terms \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     The spot market versus the trading band \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Reporting by Lu Jianxin and Pete Sweeney; Editing by\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jacqueline Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-7T05:07:54.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150907eb970048y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
