\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong Stocks Advance, Awaiting China  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Reserves -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 2,049 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2015\par 06:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0421 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Hong Kong equities ducked and weaved between gains and losses in the morning session as markets digested Friday's US jobs report as well as Chinese GDP revisions for 2014 which showed Asia's largest economy grew slightly more slowly than thought last year. Markets remain on tenterhooks for China's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve data. "With reserve assets of some US$3.6 trillion, China has ample liquidity provisions--as long as the battle doesn't get too protracted," writes Anthony Chan, Asian sovereign strategist at Bernstein. However, he also warns that efforts to ensure market stability may mark a backward step for reform, while "conducting a tug-of-war with market forces can be a long-drawn process." The \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2  Index climbs 0.2% to 20,885.74, while H-shares advance, outperforming the 0.9% gain in the Shanghai Composite. The \uc2 Hang Seng\uc2 China Enterprises\uc2  Index is up 1.9% to 9,344.02, with raw materials stocks leading gains. (gregor.hunter@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2  @gregorhunter) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0421 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Rupiah's slide to a 17-year low is credit negative for Indonesian property developers, as two thirds of their debt is denominated in US dollars but their earnings are entirely in rupiah, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . With the US dollar/rupiah exchange rate now at 14,181--the weakest since 1998--only about 20% of the developers' total U.S. dollar debt is protected by hedging facilities, according to the rating agency. In a sensitivity test that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  conducted to assess the developers' resistance to further rupiah depreciation at various levels, only one of five of its rated developers was able to withstand further rupiah depreciation to as low as 15,500 without risking a downgrade, it says. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lippo Karawaci\f28 \uc2 \f2  (LPKR.JK) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alam Sutera Realty\f28 \uc2 \f2  (ASRI.JK) are particularly vulnerable to further rupiah declines, given that their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedging facilities provide coverage only when the rupiah exchange rate is below 14,000, it adds. Still, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects the developers to maintain healthy liquidity profiles over the next 12 months, because of their strong cash positions and solid cash flows. (carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0354 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China's securities regulator is studying the possibility of a "circuit breaker" mechanism to ease market volatility as part of the latest official efforts to tame market turbulence. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Securities Regulatory Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Sunday that it is drafting a "circuit breaker" system for the main stock index, while strictly controlling program trading, curbing speculative trading of index futures, and improving regulations on margin lending, according to a statement published on its official website. Under the proposed regime, stock exchanges could invoke the circuit breaker system to halt trading should share prices exceed pre-determined ranges. Analysts say that China already has a partial circuit breaker system in place: it has imposed--since January 2014--a 44% upper limit for newly-listed stocks. However, the regulator now aims to broaden the rule for the main index. "China is learning from developed markets, which have introduced the circuit breaker system a long time ago," said Fu Xuejun, analyst at Huarong Securities. The measures come as the Shanghai market has plunged nearly 40% from its peak in mid-June. (Yifan.xie@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0345 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysis shows a larger increase in new 90+ day loan delinquencies at Chinese banks than previously reported. The Chinese commercial banking sector reported a non-performing loan (NPL) ratio of 1.50% as of June 30, which represented a moderate 25 basis-point deterioration since year end 2014. However, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes an increasing amount of loans overdue at least 90 days are not classified as non-performing by the 11 listed Chinese banks it rates. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  finds that new loans 90+ day delinquent (before write-offs and the sale of problem loans) averaged 1.54% of average loans on an annualized base for the first half of 2015, and ranged for the individual banks between 1.24% and 3.57%. The 1.54% represented a 77 basis point deterioration from the 0.77% seen in 2014. "Increasingly higher 90+ day delinquencies have led to lower loss-reserve coverage ratios for most banks, although such ratios are still at good levels," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . It expects Chinese banks' asset quality and interest margins will continue come under increasing pressure over the next 1-2 years as China's economic growth slows.(carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0339 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  says the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 's designating the country's largest state-run bank by assets, \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500112.BY) and the largest private-sector bank by assets, \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICICI Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (532174.BY) as domestic systemically important banks or banks too big too fail, is negative for other banks. RBI's implementation of just two banks shows the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is less stringent than that of other jurisdictions; a direct correlation to the capital stress that banks in India are currently experiencing. It expects \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICICI Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to be able to meet the new capital requirement whereas \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to face more of a challenge in meeting higher capital requirements. (kenan.machado@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0320 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The root cause of the recent stock market selloffs is the question of the sustainability of easing policies taken by global central banks, says Hajime Kitano, chief equity strategist at Barclays Securities Japan. He says it is, therefore, unlikely that stocks will resume their rising trends. Since the global financial crisis in 2008, major central banks around the world have resorted to unconventional monetary policies, often leading to declines of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . China's effective devaluation of the yuan, which is often cited as a culprit of the recent market routs, has triggered that question of sustainability, he says. Nikkei is down 0.4% at 17727.90 mid-day. Nikkei is only up 1.6% year to date but still 13% higher from the level prior to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's additional easing at the end of October 2014.(kosaku.narioka@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0313 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/THB has been stable near its last close of 35.96 but is biased higher as long as it stays inside the Bollinger uptrend channel - a bullish technical signal that supports the pair at 35.83. A Monday close above the round-figure trading barrier of 36.00 could cement bullish potential for USD/THB. The U.S. dollar is broadly stronger after Friday's mixed U.S. non-farm payrolls report; the reaction in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets suggests most traders believe it won't alter the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's inclination toward raising interest rates this month. Adding to bearishness for Asian emerging market assets - thereby bullishness for USD/Asia - is the return of investor anxiety after China revised lower last year's GDP numbers to show the economy grew 7.3% instead of 7.4% - a sign that the Chinese economy may be performing even worse than current data indicates. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0310 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves likely fell by $100 billion to $150 billion in August, but "only a fraction of the money actually flowed out of China," Macquarie economist Larry Hu says in a report forecasting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves data due Monday. The money was simply exchanged from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deposits in China's commercial banks, he says. But, importantly, the current pace of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves depletion doesn't predict what will happen over the next few months, "as the selloff pressure would ease if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could stabilize depreciation expectations," he writes. "We believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is credible, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves owned by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  could enable it to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  not for months, but for years..." Meanwhile, an ING analyst says the question of how much foreign reserves declined could be "potentially momentous." (dominique.fong@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0306 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Post-July, amid slumping oil prices, bonds issued by Chinese oil firms have been one of Asia's worst performing credit sectors. But valuations of some bonds, especially those issued by China's three oil majors--CNPC, Sinopec (0386.HK) and Cnooc (0883.HK) and their subsidiaries--have become attractive, says BOC International. The latest interim results confirm these Chinese oil giants remain fundamentally sound, with gearing ratios have remained largely stable and free cash flows relatively strong. At the same time, the bonds continue to trade cheaply relative to global peers, with the yield spread about 63 basis points higher than their peers in the AA- rating category. "As the global credit market continues to see elevated volatility, these high-quality Chinese credits should remain choices of defensive play," BOCI analysts say. In particular, the team likes Cnooc's 4.25% bonds due 2021 and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kunlun Energy\f28 \uc2 \f2 's (0135.HK) 2.875% bonds due 2020. (carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0300 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Saxo Capital Market's macro strategist Kay Van-Petersen is one of the few making the case for US interest rates rising in September. He says in a note to clients that revised data showing greater job gains in June and July, a solid three-month average gain of 220,000 jobs and a 5.1% unemployment rate in the US leave him "feeling very confident about a September 16 lift-off." Investors in Hong Kong at first reacted positively to the US jobs report released after Asian markets closed Friday, with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index rising as much as 1% Monday near the market open. It is now down 0.5%. "With the Fed implied probability of rate hike being 30% for September, I am clearly in the minority," says. "I also think a lot of the nervousness is around the uncertainty, the sooner we hike--whether it's one & down, or a gradual wait and see--the sooner we can move onto the next thing." (dominique.fong@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7 Sep 2015 00:21 ET \par Hong Kong Stocks Advance, Awaiting China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0259 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vinda International\f28 \uc2 \f2  (3331.HK) are weighed by concerns over the company's possible restructuring with its major shareholder--Sweden's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Svenska Cellulosa\f28 \uc2 \f2  (SCA-B.SK). The stock is down 2.2% at HK$14.44. China's major tissue-paper maker says it has mandated \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  to assist it in conducting a strategic review of its business. The results of the strategic review could lead to enhancing cooperation or combining its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia with that of the Stockholm-headquartered hygiene and forest-products company, it says. Vinda is also in initial talks to buy two plots of land together with factory facilities in southern China's Guangdong province. Vinda currently leases the sites for its major production facilities. (joanne.chiu@wsj.com, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @joannechiuhk) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: ALP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0250 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/Asia pairs have rebounded, after subsiding from a strong opening, on headlines of China cutting its 2014 gross domestic growth to 7.3% from the 7.4% expansion initially estimated. The whipsaw higher in USD/Asia represents a weakening of Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  versus the U.S. dollar. The safe haven greenback started Monday on a strong footing on bets that Friday's mixed U.S. non-farm payrolls report would not alter the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's inclination toward raising interest rates this month. But USD/Asia then retreated on a statement from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  that the government is increasing its planned government spending to 10% from 7% so as to buffer against economic slowdown. Now, investor anxiety has resurfaced with the downgraded revision of last year's GDP numbers - a sign that the Chinese economy may be performing even worse than current data indicates. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 07, 2015 00:21 ET (04:21 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150907eb9700088\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
