\par\par \b \uc2 US CREDIT OPEN-Markets uncertain as US stock futures firm\b0\par\par\uc2 By Mike Gambale   \par \uc2 918 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2015\par 14:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 2 (IFR) - Summary of overnight events and Wednesday's main headlines:\par \par \uc2 Dow Futures: +124, \uc2 S&P\uc2  Futures: +13.75, \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  Futures: +32.00\par \par \uc2 CDX IG24: +1.252bp tighter, CDX HY24: -0.2820 point higher\par \par \uc2 10-yr \uc2 UST\uc2  yield: 2.158% -1.4bp; 30-yr \uc2 UST\uc2  yield: 2.920%, -1.2bp\par \par \uc2 EUR/USD: 1.1266, +0.43%\par \par \uc2 HEADLINES\par \par \uc2 FUTURES UP AS CHINA FEARS EASE\par \par \uc2 U.S. stock index futures rose on Wednesday after fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its markets helped calm jittery investors, and ahead of U.S. private employment data.\par \par \uc2 CHINA SETS RESERVES FOR \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  DERIVATIVES\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will require reserves to be set aside for purchases of all \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives from October, according to a document seen by Reuters, as Beijing moves to make it more expensive to bet on further depreciation of the yuan.\par \par \uc2 FED COULD CAUSE INSTABILITY: GROSS\par \par \uc2 Bond guru Bill Gross, who has long called for the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to raise interest rates, said on Wednesday that U.S. central bankers may have missed their window of opportunity to hike rates earlier this year and normalizing them now could create "self-inflicted financial instability."\par \par \uc2 PUERTO RICO DEAL FOR BONDHOLDERS\par \par \uc2 Puerto Rico's indebted public utility PREPA has reached a deal with a key bondholder group which would see them swap their bonds for new notes, receiving 85 percent of their existing bond claims, according to a statement from the utility.\par \par \uc2 US MORTGAGE APPLICATIONS UP\par \par \uc2 Applications for U.S. home mortgages rose last week as both purchase and refinancing applications jumped, an industry group said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MACRO\par \par \uc2 - Market opens risk-off but bounces as calmer markets expected ahead of China holidays\par \par \uc2 - Shanghai Composite loses 0.37%\par \par \uc2 - NIKKEI loses 0.39% on continued global growth concerns\par \par \uc2 - Brent crude loses some of recent gains on China and oversupply concerns, last at $48\par \par \uc2 - UK Markit/CIPS Construction PMI 57.3 (exp 57.5, prev 57.1)\par \par \uc2 - EZ July Producer Prices -0.1% m/m (exp -0.1, prev -0) and -2.1% y/y (exp -2.1, prev -2.1)\par \par \uc2 - FTSE moves 0.12% higher on improved corporate results\par \par \uc2 - COMMENT: ECB - Draghi unlikely to rock the boat [ID: nIFR7pbCPV]\par \par \uc2 - The tactical bias is that of a defensive range trader favoring selling strength out the curve while buying weakness in the belly\par \par \uc2 - 10s trade in a range of 2.170% and 2.145% overnight\par \par \uc2 - Look for a 2.23% to 2.13% range in 10s\par \par \uc2 US DATA\par \par \uc2 - 07:00 MBA Weekly Mortgage Application Activity Indices\par \par \uc2 - 08:15 \uc2 ADP\uc2  National Employment Report (Aug) (mkt +201k, prev +185k)\par \par \uc2 - 08:30 Productivity (Q2 revised) (mkt +2.8% q/q AR, prev +1.3% q/q AR)\par \par \uc2 - 08:30 Unit Labor Costs (Q2 revised) (mkt -1.0% q/q AR, prev +0.5% q/q AR)\par \par \uc2 - 10:00 Factory Orders (Jul) (mkt +0.9% m/m, prev +1.8% m/m)\par \par \uc2 - 10:00 -- Factory Orders ex-Transportation (Jul) (prev +0.5% m/m)\par \par \uc2 - 10:30 EIA Weekly Petroleum Statistics\par \par \uc2 EVENTS\par \par \uc2 - 11:45 FedTrade \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  30-year \uc2 Fannie Mae\uc2  / \uc2 Freddie Mac\uc2  (max $2.025 bn)\par \par \uc2 - 14:00 Beige Book\par \par \uc2 HIGH-GRADE SUMMARY\par \par \uc2 August issuance volume: US$49.775bn\par \par \uc2 Quarterly issuance volume: US$182.027bn\par \par \uc2 2015 issuance volume: US$900.202bn\par \par \uc2 Sept 2014 issuance volume: US$128.718bn\par \par \uc2 USD HIGH-GRADE PIPELINE\par \par \uc2 Korea Development Bank\uc2  (Aa3/A+/AA-) has mandated \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2 , \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 , \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2 , \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 , KDB Asia, \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2  and \uc2 UBS\uc2  as joint bookrunners for a US dollar bond. Kick-off meetings began on August 27. KDB was last in the dollar market in May with a US$500m offering of 5-year bonds, priced at 72.5bp over US Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 Tyco International\uc2  mandates DB, GS and MS to arrange a series of fixed income investor calls. GS is coordinating the calls.\par \par \uc2 Corporacion Andina de Fomento\uc2  (CAF), Aa3/AA-, filed a $3b debt securities shelf registration, including $500mm existing. Proceeds were earmarked for fund lending \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Korea National Oil Corporation\uc2 , Aa3/AA-, mandated \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , KDB and \uc2 UBS\uc2  to arrange fixed income investor meetings in the U.S., Asia and Europe. A transaction could soon follow the conclusion of the meetings.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \uc2 Pertamina\uc2  has mandated \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 , \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  and \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  to arrange an offering of US dollar 144A/Reg S offering, but pricing, timing and tenors have yet to be decided, according to sources close to the company.\par \par \uc2 Thai Oil Public Company Limited\uc2 , Baa1/BBB, mandated \uc2 HSBC\uc2  and \uc2 Standard Chartered Bank\uc2  to assist in a $1bn GMTN Program established on June 26th. The Company will meet with investors in the U.S., Asia and Europe.\par \par \uc2 San Diego Gas & Electric Co\uc2 , Aa2/A+, filed a $1.14b S-3 shelf registration statement covering Senior debt securities, First Mortgage Bonds and Preferred stock bringing its total available shelf to $1.5b. Use of proceeds will be applied toward expanding and improving its utility plants, to refund and retire indebtedness, for working capital and other general corporate purposes and to replenish funds previously expended for those purposes.\par \par \uc2 British Telecommunications plc\uc2 , Baa2/BBB, filed a form F-3 shelf registration statement covering debt securities with use of proceeds designated for general corporate purposes. (Reporting by Michael Gambale; Editing by Marc Carnegie)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-5T12:10:56.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150902eb9200fid\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
