\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan firms on suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , tighter forwards rules\b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2015\par 07:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Sept 1 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan firmed on Tuesday\par as state-owned banks were suspected of selling dollars at the\par central banks behest, and sources told Reuters that authorities\par were preparing to tighten rules on forwards trading to deter\par speculation against the yuan, traders said.\par     "Some state-owned banks still bought yuan in the morning\par trade," said a trader at a Chinese commercial bank in Shanghai,\par "However, such purchases were not as much as on Monday and last\par Friday."\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.3752 per dollar prior to market open, 0.22 percent firmer\par than the previous fix 6.3893. It is the third day in a row that\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised the midpoint rate.\par     Spot yuan opened at 6.3750 per dollar and was\par changing hands at 6.3698 at midday, up 0.1 percent from the\par previous close, reaching its strongest level since a devaluation\par on Aug. 11.\par     Traders believed that the yuan is on track to stabilise\par around 6.4 per dollar.\par     The offshore yuan weakened 0.4 percent in morning\par trade and was trading 0.7 percent down from the onshore spot at\par 6.415 per dollar.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will tighten rules on trading of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forwards from next month, sources with direct knowledge\par of the matter told Reuters on Tuesday, in a move to curb\par speculation and rising volatility after a sharp sell-off in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     "It's partly a move to strike hard at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  arbitrage\par activity," said a trader at a foreign bank in Shanghai. "It\par effectively deters speculation on further yuan depreciation."\par     A survey published on Tuesday showed factory activity in\par China had deteriorated last month. The official Purchasing\par Managers' Index (PMI) fell to 49.7 in August from the previous\par month's reading of 50.0. The final Caixin/Markit Manufacturing\par PMI also dropped.  \par     Traders said the data had little impact on trading.\par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts\par , considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 6.5825, or 3.15 percent weaker than the midpoint.\par     \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.3752   6.3893    0.22%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.3698   6.3763    0.10%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    -0.08%             \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -2.60%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.93%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.415     -0.70%\par           *                      \par  Offshore              6.5825    -3.15%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     GRAPHICS:\par     The yuan in trade-weighted terms \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     The spot market versus the trading band \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par  \par   \par \par \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Simon\par Cameron-Moore)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-1T06:03:28.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150901eb91005io\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
