\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan weakens as stock market extends decline\b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2015\par 06:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI Aug 25 (Reuters) - China's yuan dipped against the\par dollar on Tuesday after closing at its weakest level since 2011\par on Monday, hit by another slump in the mainland's stock market\par and a weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  midpoint.\par     Traders said they believed the yuan's current range between\par 6.29 and 6.43 to the dollar was well accepted by the market\par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent volatility once threatened a sharper\par depreciation.\par     "The yuan is unlikely to depreciate to 6.50," said a trader\par at a foreign bank in Shanghai, adding that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par likely to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow down the depreciation.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's major stock indexes slumped more than 6 percent to\par 8-month lows in early trade on Tuesday before paring some losses\par by midday, continuing a recent rout. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint rate\par  at 6.3987 per dollar prior to market open, 0.2\par percent weaker than the previous fix of 6.3862.\par     The spot market opened at 6.4149 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.4109 at midday, 0.1 percent weaker than\par the previous close.\par     Offshore yuan was trading 0.92 percent weaker than\par the onshore spot at 6.4705 per dollar by midday.\par     "The stock market crash provoked concerns about China's\par slack economy," said a trader at an Asian bank in Hong Kong.\par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts\par , considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 6.6975, 4.46 percent weaker than the midpoint.\par   \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint      6.3987   6.3862    -0.20%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.4109   6.4044    -0.10%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.19%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change ytd                       -3.23%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.10%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.4705    -0.92%\par           *                      \par  Offshore              6.6975    -4.46%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     GRAPHICS:\par     The yuan in trade-weighted terms \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     The spot market versus the trading band \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Reporting by Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jacqueline Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-25T05:28:13.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150825eb8p004pv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
