\par\par \b \uc2 ING-In 90 seconds - what the cheaper Chinese yuan means for Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2015\par \uc2 ENP Newswire\par \uc2 ENPNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2015, Electronic News Publishing. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 Release date - 20082015\par \par \uc2 Even if you're not planning to visit China, the surprise depreciation of the Chinese yuan this month is important, ING economists say.\par \par \uc2 In the August 2015 economic update video for eZonomics, ING senior economist Bert Colijn tells how the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed policy in early August. 'The official explanation is that they want markets to influence the price of the yuan more.'\par \par \uc2 Colijn says the Chinese economy had been suffering from deteriorating growth and a stock market crash.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the yuan - record its sharpest depreciation against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the mid-1990s.\par \par \uc2 'Because of the depreciation, your 'made in China' products will become cheaper,' he says. 'The other side of the coin is that business owners selling to China could see a negative effect on sales, as imports become more expensive for the Chinese.'\par \par \uc2 In past years, several countries have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets - but, when used in the extreme, 'competitive devaluations' can risk sparking a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in China has two names, as the BBC explains. The yuan is the name of the unit (similar to pounds in the UK), while the renminbi is the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official name (similar to sterling in the UK).\par \par \uc2 Effects on other countries and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  vary\par \par \uc2 Colijn says the extent of the depreciation is not yet fully known, but the effects could possibly be far-reaching.\par \par \uc2 'Stock markets and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially in emerging markets could weaken. It could even influence the timing of increases in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in the US and UK, although this is not the scenario currently deemed most likely.'\par \par \uc2 [Editorial queries for this story should be sent to newswire@enpublishing.co.uk]\par \par \uc2 Dokument ENPNEW0020150821eb8l00021\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
