\par\par \b \uc2 China's Weak Economic Data to Further Drive Yuan Down: BNP -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2015\par 07:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Korean (English)\par \uc2 RTNWK\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0401 GMT [Dow Jones] China's weakening economic data could further drive down the yuan as Beijing gives the market a bigger role in determining the price of the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Jacqueline Rong, economist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . But the yuan is unlikely to see any further large devaluations like it experienced last week, added Rong, as \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will still continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there are big swings. She also says the likelihood for the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  to lower reserve requirement ratios for banks is rising, given a lower-than-expected manufacturing PMI reading and capital outflows. Rong also says that she won't be surprised that the RRR in the next 3 years declines to the 10% level, down from the current level of 18.5% for big banks. (grace.zhu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Editor: JFN\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 21, 2015 00:01 ET (04:01 GMT)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 21-08-15 0550GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNWK00020150821eb8l0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
