\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan flat after suspected \uc2 PBOC \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2015\par 05:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Aug 14 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan held steady\par against the dollar on Friday after suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to get the volatile market to settle into a range\par and to curb expectations that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will fall into a\par depreciation cycle.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the yuan's midpoint rate\par  at 6.3975 per dollar prior to market open, firmer\par than the previous fix at 6.401.\par     The spot market opened at 6.3990 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.3995 at midday, 5 pips away from the\par previous close and 0.03 percent away from the midpoint.\par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade within a range 2\par percent above or below the official fixing on any given day.\par     The yuan fell for three consecutive days and had repeatedly\par touched fresh four-year lows since Tuesday, when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's\par Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 surprised the market by devaluing the yuan\par by nearly 2 percent.\par     "Major state banks are suspected of buying yuan whenever it\par nears 6.4 per dollar. This level appears to be where the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par wants to keep the yuan stable for today, possibly in the near\par term," said a trader at a foreign bank in Shanghai.\par     PBOC Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yi Gang\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Thursday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par had already withdrawn from regular \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but would\par implement effective management of the exchange rate in case of\par extreme \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility. \par     Offshore yuan was trading at 6.4325 per dollar, 0.51 percent\par away from the onshore spot rate.\par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts\par (NDFs), considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 6.5425, or 2.22 percent away from the midpoint.\par     One-year NDFs are settled against the midpoint, not the spot\par rate, and now that the trading band has been widened to 2\par percent in either direction, corporates are much more wary of\par using NDFs to hedge, given the basis risk inherent in them.\par     As a result, the market has lost liquidity in recent years\par and has frequently proven an unreliable measure of market\par sentiment.\par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item                        Current  Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.3975   6.401     0.05%\par  Spot yuan                   6.3995   6.399     -0.01%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   0.03%              \par  Spot change ytd                                -3.05%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation             29.33%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument                    Current   Difference\par                                          from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan        *   6.4325    -0.51%\par  Offshore non-deliverable      6.5425    -2.22%\par  forwards               **               \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     GRAPHICS:\par     The yuan in trade-weighted terms \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     The spot market versus the trading band \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://reut.rs/1MhsqOi}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Reporting by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michelle Chen\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Lu Jianxin; Editing by Edmund\par Klamann)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-14T04:23:00.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150814eb8e003mm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
