\par\par \b \uc2 RUBBER-Tokyo futures inch lower, set for flat week on China caution\b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2015\par 03:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 14 (Reuters) - Benchmark TOCOM rubber futures inched lower on Friday on weaker oil prices and were heading for a flat week as traders remain cautious over China even after its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reassured there was no reason for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep falling.\par \par \uc2 FUNDAMENTALS\par \par \uc2 * The Tokyo Commodity Exchange rubber contract for January delivery <0#2JRU:> was down 1.0 yen, or 0.5 percent, at 193.3 yen per kg at 0054 GMT, after finishing 0.2 yen higher the previous day.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday there was no reason for the yuan to fall further given the country's strong economic fundamentals, helping to restore calm to global markets after it devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in yuan trading, ordering state banks to buy yuan at designated rates on behalf of the monetary authorities, among other emergency measures, banking sources with direct knowledge of the matter told Reuters on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 * U.S. retail sales rebounded in July as households boosted purchases of automobiles and a range of other goods, suggesting the economy was growing solidly early in the third quarter and bolstering the case for a \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  interest rate hike.\par \par \uc2 * For the top stories in the rubber market and other news, click or\par \par \uc2 MARKET NEWS\par \par \uc2 * U.S. oil prices tumbled more than 3 percent to a 6-1/2-year low under $42 a barrel on Thursday as data showing a big rise in key U.S. stockpiles intensified worries over a growing global glut.\par \par \uc2 * Copper steadied on Thursday above the previous session's six-year low after \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said there was no basis for further yuan depreciation, dampening concerns that the country's appetite for metals imports could wane.\par \par \uc2 * The U.S. dollar was quoted around 124.40 yen early on Friday.\par \par \uc2 * Japan's benchmark Nikkei stock average was down 0.4 percent in Friday trade, after U.S. equities, which had rebounded from steep losses Wednesday, were mixed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 DATA/EVENTS (GMT)\par \par \uc2 * The following data is expected on Friday: (Time in GMT)\par \par \uc2 0600 Germany GDP Q2\par \par \uc2 0900 Euro zone GDP Q2\par \par \uc2 0900 Euro zone Inflation final Jul\par \par \uc2 1315 U.S. Industrial output Jul\par \par \uc2 1400 U.S. Univ of Michigan sentiment index Aug\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Yuka \uc2 Obayashi\uc2 ; Editing by Ed Davies) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-14T02:14:57.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150814eb8e001gz\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (china near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw)and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trg